## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical CAPA design skills: data modeling, lifecycle governance, lightweight APIs, and measurable containment strategies in a multi-tenant, multi-region setup.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model tailored to tenants/regions
- Lifecycle state machine with auditable transitions
- Minimal REST API for creating/updating CAPAs with evidence
- Region/tenant-aware metrics to prove containment
- RCA template and canary remediation plan

## Code Example
```javascript
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  tenants: string[];
  regions: string[];
  evidence: string[];
  batchInfo: {
    schedule: string;
    duration: number;
    resources: string[];
  };
  rootCause: string;
  corrective: string;
  preventive: string;
  owner: string;
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
};

// Lifecycle states
type CAPAState = 'Identified' | 'Contained' | 'Investigating' | 'Corrected' | 'Verified';

// REST API endpoints
POST /capas
PUT /capas/:id
GET /capas?tenant=:t&region=:r&state=:s
```

## Metrics & Containment
- Tenant/region latency percentiles pre/post containment
- Batch job resource utilization by tenant/region
- Error rates and success rates during remediation
- Canary deployment success metrics by region

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design practical CAPA governance tied to real-time data flows and multi-tenant risk without overengineering.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model fields (id, tenant_ids, sink, data_classification, evidence, region, remediation_links, state)
- Region-aware lifecycle states
- Minimal REST API (POST /caps, PATCH /caps/{id})
- Metrics: recurrence_rate, MTTR, false_positives, containment_time per region
- RCA template and safe-canary rollback plan

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express endpoints for CAPA creation
const app = require('express')();
app.use(express.json());
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => { /* create CAPA */ res.status(201).send({ id: 'capa-123' }); });
app.patch('/caps/:id', (req, res) => { /* update CAPA */ res.status(200).send({ ok: true }); });
```

## Why This Is Asked
New angle focusing on synthetic data leakage in cross-tenant data sharing, a realistic risk in data marketplaces. Tests ability to model data lineage, region-specific containment, and a safe rollout.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence, tenantIDs, sourceDataset, generatorVersion
- Region-aware lifecycle and canary rollout
- Metrics: leakageRate, MTTR, false positives; RCA template

## Code Example
```javascript
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
let capas = [];
app.post('/capas', (req, res) => {
  const c = req.body; c.id = Date.now().toString();
  capas.push(c); res.status(201).json(c);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you aggregate region-specific leakage metrics across data-sharing tenants?  
- What privacy controls would you enforce in the CAPA lifecycle and RCA templates?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design end-to-end CAPA for a hardware-leaning, safety-critical system with OTA risk, cross-region data, and telemetry traces. Emphasizes traceability, regionalization, and safe validation.

## Key Concepts
- Immutable evidence ledger (incidentId, firmwareVersion, OTA bundle, sensor flags, region, vehicle_type)
- Region-aware CAPA lifecycle state machine
- Minimal REST API to link CAPAs with logs/traces
- Region- and vehicle-type metrics: recurrence rate, MTTR, false-positive rate
- RCA template and canary rollout with rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express route to create a CAPA
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
app.post('/capa', (req, res) => {
  const { incidentId, firmwareVersion, otaBundle, region, vehicleType, evidenceLinks } = req.body;
  // Persist CAPA object with linked evidence in DB (pseudo)
  const capaId = generateId();
  saveCapa({ capaId, incidentId, firmwareVersion, otaBundle, region, vehicleType, evidenceLinks, status: 'DETECTED' });
  res.status(201).json({ id: capaId });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you model cross-region deduplication of CAPAs when two regions report the same incident?
- What metrics and experiments would verify the efficacy of the canary rollout before global deployment?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end CAPA design focusing on data-feed integrity and cross-region policy latency.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with provenance for logs/traces
- Region-aware lifecycle and state transitions
- REST API linking CAPAs to evidence logs/traces
- Region-aware metrics: MTTR, recurrence, false positives, latency
- RCA template and canary rollout plan for policy updates

## Code Example
```javascript
interface CAPA {
  id: string;
  incidentId: string;
  region: string;
  tenantId: string;
  policyVersion: string;
  evidence: string[]; // logs/traces
  state: 'identified'|'investigating'|'contained'|'mitigated'|'closed';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
  remediation?: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate data-feed integrity across regions during rollback?
- What trade-offs exist between rapid containment and thorough RCA in high-throughput systems?
